yaml/boolean
description: The literals true and false, three casings each
- >
  A boolean is one of the literals `true` and `false` — also accepted Capitalized and in ALL
  CAPS. A SUPERCLASS of
  [json/boolean](::language:01-Concretes_2:04-json_code:01-json_scalar:02-json_boolean), which
  knows the lowercase pair only:
- !!<format: text/x-yaml> |
  a: true
  b: False
  c: TRUE
- *..:..:..:..:04-json_code:01-json_scalar:02-json_boolean
